<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Checklist</h3>

<div id="Sx1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="Sx1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Sx1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all models and algorithms presented, check if you include:</p>
<ol id="Sx1.I1.i1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Sx1.I1.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A clear description of the mathematical setting, assumptions, algorithm, and/or model. Yes</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An analysis of the properties and complexity (time, space, sample size) of any algorithm. Not Applicable</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(Optional) Anonymized source code, with specification of all dependencies, including external libraries. Yes, anonymized source code, including instructions for optimal reproducibility, is included in the supplementary material.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any theoretical claim, check if you include:</p>
<ol id="Sx1.I1.i2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Sx1.I1.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Statements of the full set of assumptions of all theoretical results. Yes</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Complete proofs of all theoretical results. Yes</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Clear explanations of any assumptions. Yes</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all figures and tables that present empirical results, check if you include:</p>
<ol id="Sx1.I1.i3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Sx1.I1.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The code, data, and instructions needed to reproduce the main experimental results (either in the supplemental material or as a URL). Yes</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All the training details (e.g., data splits, hyperparameters, how they were chosen). Yes</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A clear definition of the specific measure or statistics and error bars (e.g., with respect to the random seed after running experiments multiple times). Yes</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(d)</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A description of the computing infrastructure used. (e.g., type of GPUs, internal cluster, or cloud provider). Yes</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If you are using existing assets (e.g., code, data, models) or curating/releasing new assets, check if you include:</p>
<ol id="Sx1.I1.i4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Sx1.I1.i4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Citations of the creator If your work uses existing assets. Yes</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The license information of the assets, if applicable. Yes</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">New assets either in the supplemental material or as a URL, if applicable. Yes</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(d)</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Information about consent from data providers/curators. Not Applicable</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i4.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(e)</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i4.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i4.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Discussion of sensible content if applicable, e.g., personally identifiable information or offensive content. Not Applicable</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If you used crowdsourcing or conducted research with human subjects, check if you include:</p>
<ol id="Sx1.I1.i5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Sx1.I1.i5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The full text of instructions given to participants and screenshots. Not Applicable</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Descriptions of potential participant risks, with links to Institutional Review Board (IRB) approvals if applicable. Not Applicable</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The estimated hourly wage paid to participants and the total amount spent on participant compensation. Not Applicable</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:4.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
<div id="Sx1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent ltx_align_center">
<p id="Sx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PENEX: AdaBoost-Inspired 
<br class="ltx_break">Neural Network Regularization 
<br class="ltx_break">Supplementary Materials</span></p>
</div><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
</section>
<section id="Pt1" class="ltx_part">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_part">Appendix</h2>

<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs</h3>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof for <a href="#S2.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 2.1 (Fisher Consistency). ‣ 2.1 Theoretical Properties ‣ 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Prop.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a></h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We consider the following blueprint:</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We show that PENEX is Fisher consistent, conditionally on any <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and for any <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We show that PENEX is also unconditionally Fisher consistent.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><a href="#A1.I1.i1" title="In Proof. ‣ A.1 Proof for ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Step</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h6>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The population-level equivalent of <a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, conditionally on <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, is</p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}^{y|\mathbf{x}}(f(\mathbf{x}))\;\coloneqq\;\mathbb{E}_{y|\mathbf{x}}\Big[\exp\Big\{-\alpha f^{(y)}(\mathbf{x})\Big\}\Big]\;+\;\rho\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\Big\{f^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\Big\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">PENEX</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}^{y|\mathbf{x}}(f(\mathbf{x}))\;\coloneqq\;\mathbb{E}_{y|\mathbf{x}}\Big[\exp\Big\{-\alpha f^{(y)}(\mathbf{x})\Big\}\Big]\;+\;\rho\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\Big\{f^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\Big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We note that <a href="#A1.E11" title="In A.1 Proof for ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> is strictly convex in <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> and differentiable. Hence, the unique minimum of <a href="#A1.E11" title="In A.1 Proof for ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, called <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{*}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{*}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>, is characterized by its gradient being zero:</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}^{y|\mathbf{x}}}{\partial f_{*}^{(y)}(\mathbf{x})}\;=\;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">PENEX</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em">=</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}^{y|\mathbf{x}}}{\partial f_{*}^{(y)}(\mathbf{x})}\;=\;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which leads to</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(y\,|\,\mathbf{x})\;=\;\frac{\rho}{\alpha}\exp\left\{(1+\alpha)f_{*}^{(y)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(y\,|\,\mathbf{x})\;=\;\frac{\rho}{\alpha}\exp\left\{(1+\alpha)f_{*}^{(y)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Due to re-normalization, the factor <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho/\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho/\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is canceled out and hence, the result follows.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><a href="#A1.I1.i2" title="In Proof. ‣ A.1 Proof for ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Step</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h6>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">First, we note that the specific choice of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> does not matter for the result shown in <a href="#A1.I1.i1" title="In Proof. ‣ A.1 Proof for ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Step</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, due to re-normalization. Consequently, we can pick a single, arbitrary <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> that achieves Fisher consistency for all <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>. We now consider the unconditional population equivalent of PENEX <a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>,</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E13X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}(f)\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}}\left[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}^{y|\mathbf{x}}(f(\mathbf{x}))\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">PENEX</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">PENEX</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}(f)\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}}\left[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}^{y|\mathbf{x}}(f(\mathbf{x}))\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">It is easy to see that its minimizer is given by the function <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> that minimizes the conditional PENEX <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}^{y|\mathbf{x}}(f(\mathbf{x}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">PENEX</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}^{y|\mathbf{x}}(f(\mathbf{x}))</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\in\text{supp}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\in\text{supp}(P)</annotation></semantics></math> <a href="#A1.E11" title="In A.1 Proof for ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>. We consider an arbitrary function <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> and see that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}(f)]-\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}(f_{*})]=\int_{\mathbf{x}\in\text{supp}(P)}\left[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}^{y|\mathbf{x}}(f(\mathbf{x}))-\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}^{y|\mathbf{x}}(f_{*}(\mathbf{x}))\right]p(\mathbf{x})d\mathbf{x}\geq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">PENEX</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">PENEX</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">PENEX</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">PENEX</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}(f)]-\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}(f_{*})]=\int_{\mathbf{x}\in\text{supp}(P)}\left[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}^{y|\mathbf{x}}(f(\mathbf{x}))-\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}^{y|\mathbf{x}}(f_{*}(\mathbf{x}))\right]p(\mathbf{x})d\mathbf{x}\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">which concludes the proof.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof for <a href="#S2.Thmobservation1" title="Observation 2.1. ‣ 2.1 Theoretical Properties ‣ 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Obs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a></h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">For simplicity, we assume that <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> can only take one single value, such that estimating <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(Y\,|\,X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(Y\,|\,X)</annotation></semantics></math> simplifies to estimating the parameters of a multinoulli/categorical distribution, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(y)</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, we note that we make can make statements about the estimated <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> by solving for <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}</annotation></semantics></math> instead, since <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}(y)\propto\exp\left\{f^{(y)}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}(y)\propto\exp\left\{f^{(y)}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> constrains <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> up to an additive constant. We consider a more explicit notation for the objective <a href="#S2.E4" title="In Observation 2.1. ‣ 2.1 Theoretical Properties ‣ 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\hat{P})\;=\;H(P\,\|\,\hat{P})\;+\;\lambda\Omega(\hat{P})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\hat{P})\;=\;H(P\,\|\,\hat{P})\;+\;\lambda\Omega(\hat{P}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(P\,\|\,\hat{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(P\,\|\,\hat{P})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes cross-entropy between <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is regularization strength. With <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(P)</annotation></semantics></math> denoting Shannon entropy of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, we note that we can rewrite cross-entropy as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(P\,\|\,\hat{P})\;=\;H(P)\;+\;\text{KL}(P\,\|\,\hat{P})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(P\,\|\,\hat{P})\;=\;H(P)\;+\;\text{KL}(P\,\|\,\hat{P}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">and see that the unique optimum for the trivial case <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math> is given as <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}_{*}=P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}_{*}=P</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., Fisher consistency holds. However, this is generally not the case if <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. To see this, we construct the Lagrangian</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{L}(\hat{P})\;=\;\mathcal{L}(\hat{P})\;+\;\lambda^{\prime}\Big(\sum_{y=1}^{K}\hat{P}(y)-1\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{L}(\hat{P})\;=\;\mathcal{L}(\hat{P})\;+\;\lambda^{\prime}\Big(\sum_{y=1}^{K}\hat{P}(y)-1\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">with Lagrange multiplier <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the stationarity condition, it must hold for all <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\frac{P(y)}{\hat{P}(y)}\Bigg|_{\hat{P}(y)=\hat{P}_{*}(y)}\,+\,\lambda\frac{\partial\Omega}{\partial\hat{P}(y)}\Bigg|_{\hat{P}(y)=\hat{P}_{*}(y)}+\lambda^{\prime}\;=\;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.392em">+</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.392em">+</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\frac{P(y)}{\hat{P}(y)}\Bigg|_{\hat{P}(y)=\hat{P}_{*}(y)}\,+\,\lambda\frac{\partial\Omega}{\partial\hat{P}(y)}\Bigg|_{\hat{P}(y)=\hat{P}_{*}(y)}+\lambda^{\prime}\;=\;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">At <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}=P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}=P</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#A1.E15" title="In Proof. ‣ A.2 Proof for ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> simplifies to</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\frac{\partial\Omega}{\partial\hat{P}(y)}\;=\;1-\lambda^{\prime}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\frac{\partial\Omega}{\partial\hat{P}(y)}\;=\;1-\lambda^{\prime},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">which means that <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> can only be optimal if</span></p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\Omega}{\partial\hat{P}(y)}\Bigg|_{\hat{P}(y)=P(y)}=\text{const.},\;\forall y\in[K]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>const.</mtext></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\Omega}{\partial\hat{P}(y)}\Bigg|_{\hat{P}(y)=P(y)}=\text{const.},\;\forall y\in[K].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">It is easy to see, however, that <a href="#A1.E16" title="In Proof. ‣ A.2 Proof for ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> is generally not the case. For example, in the case of a confidence penalty <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(\hat{P})=-H(\hat{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(\hat{P})=-H(\hat{P})</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\Omega}{\partial\hat{P}(y)}\;=\;1+\log(\hat{P}(y))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\Omega}{\partial\hat{P}(y)}\;=\;1+\log(\hat{P}(y))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.8.1" class="ltx_text">and so <a href="#A1.E16" title="In Proof. ‣ A.2 Proof for ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> is true if and only if <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(y)</annotation></semantics></math> is the uniform distribution, i.e., <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(y)=K^{-1},\,\forall y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(y)=K^{-1},\,\forall y</annotation></semantics></math>. This is only true in trivial cases. The same argument applies to other choices of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(\hat{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(\hat{P})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Proof for <a href="#S2.Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 2.3. ‣ PENEX is Implicit AdaBoost. ‣ 2.3 Relationship to Multi-Class AdaBoost ‣ 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Prop.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a></h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We choose the set of functions to be</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathrm{PENEX}}\;\coloneqq\;\Bigg\{\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})\Delta\theta\;\Big|\;\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\left\{f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})+\eta(\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})\Delta\theta_{m})^{(j)}\right\}\Big]\leq\epsilon,\;\left\lVert\Delta\theta\right\rVert_{2}=1\Bigg\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">PENEX</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐉</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.280em" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐉</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathrm{PENEX}}\;\coloneqq\;\Bigg\{\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})\Delta\theta\;\Big|\;\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\left\{f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})+\eta(\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})\Delta\theta_{m})^{(j)}\right\}\Big]\leq\epsilon,\;\left\lVert\Delta\theta\right\rVert_{2}=1\Bigg\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\,\coloneqq\,\hat{\mathbb{E}}[\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\{f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.448em" rspace="0.448em">≔</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\,\coloneqq\,\hat{\mathbb{E}}[\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\{f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We start by performing a Taylor approximation of the objective function and the constraints around <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=0</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S2.E10" title="In PENEX is Implicit AdaBoost. ‣ 2.3 Relationship to Multi-Class AdaBoost ‣ 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>. This yields</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[\exp\left\{-\alpha f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(y)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}\right]-\alpha\eta\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[\exp\left\{-\alpha f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(y)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})^{(y)}\right]\Delta\theta+h_{1}(\eta,\Delta\theta)\eta" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[\exp\left\{-\alpha f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(y)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}\right]-\alpha\eta\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[\exp\left\{-\alpha f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(y)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})^{(y)}\right]\Delta\theta+h_{1}(\eta,\Delta\theta)\eta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">for the objective function and</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\left\{f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}\Big]+\eta\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\left\{f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})^{(j)}\Big]\Delta\theta+h_{2}(\eta,\Delta\theta)\eta\leq\varepsilon" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\left\{f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}\Big]+\eta\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\left\{f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})^{(j)}\Big]\Delta\theta+h_{2}(\eta,\Delta\theta)\eta\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">for the constraints, where <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{1}(\eta,\Delta\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1}(\eta,\Delta\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{2}(\eta,\Delta\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{2}(\eta,\Delta\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> are continuous functions that satisfy <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\eta\rightarrow 0}h_{1}(\eta,\Delta\theta)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\eta\rightarrow 0}h_{1}(\eta,\Delta\theta)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\eta\rightarrow 0}h_{2}(\eta,\Delta\theta)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\eta\rightarrow 0}h_{2}(\eta,\Delta\theta)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and where, by assumption,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\{f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\}\Big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\{f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\}\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">In addition, we used the notation <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math> to refer to the <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>th row of the Jacobian matrix <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐉</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>. The optimization in <a href="#S2.E10" title="In PENEX is Implicit AdaBoost. ‣ 2.3 Relationship to Multi-Class AdaBoost ‣ 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> can therefore be rewritten as</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v(\eta)\quad\coloneqq\quad\min_{\Delta\theta}-\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo>≔</mo><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v(\eta)\quad\coloneqq\quad\min_{\Delta\theta}-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[\exp\left\{-\alpha f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(y)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})^{(y)}\right]\Delta\theta+h_{1}(\eta,\Delta\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[\exp\left\{-\alpha f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(y)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})^{(y)}\right]\Delta\theta+h_{1}(\eta,\Delta\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex16.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">subject to</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\left\{f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})^{(j)}\Big]\Delta\theta+h_{2}(\eta,\Delta\theta)\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\left\{f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})^{(j)}\Big]\Delta\theta+h_{2}(\eta,\Delta\theta)\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lVert\Delta\theta\right\rVert_{2}^{2}=1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lVert\Delta\theta\right\rVert_{2}^{2}=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">For small <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, the first constraint reduces to a half-space passing through the origin. This implies that the constraint can be strictly satisfied for <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=0</annotation></semantics></math> and therefore, due to continuity, the feasible set in <a href="#S2.E10" title="In PENEX is Implicit AdaBoost. ‣ 2.3 Relationship to Multi-Class AdaBoost ‣ 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> (or equivalently <a href="#A1.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ A.3 Proof for ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) is nonempty for small enough <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>. We further note that <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math>, the minimum value in <a href="#A1.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ A.3 Proof for ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>, is continuous for small <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, see for example <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Still, 2018</a>, Ch. 5)</cite> and consider any sequence <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{k}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{k}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and corresponding <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta_{mk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta_{mk}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,2,\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,2,\dots</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{k}\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{k}\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta_{mk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta_{mk}</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to the corresponding set of minimizers of <a href="#S2.E10" title="In PENEX is Implicit AdaBoost. ‣ 2.3 Relationship to Multi-Class AdaBoost ‣ 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>. Our goal is to show that any limit point of the sequence belongs to the set of minimizer of <a href="#S2.E9" title="In PENEX is Implicit AdaBoost. ‣ 2.3 Relationship to Multi-Class AdaBoost ‣ 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> with <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=0</annotation></semantics></math>. To that extend, we first note that <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta_{mk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta_{mk}</annotation></semantics></math> remains bounded, since <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\Delta\theta_{mk}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\Delta\theta_{mk}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider any limit point <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta_{mk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta_{mk}</annotation></semantics></math> and pass to a subsequence <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta_{mk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta_{mk}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta_{mk}\rightarrow\Delta\theta_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta_{mk}\rightarrow\Delta\theta_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>. We now show that <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> is a minimizer of <a href="#S2.E10" title="In PENEX is Implicit AdaBoost. ‣ 2.3 Relationship to Multi-Class AdaBoost ‣ 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> (or equivalently <a href="#A1.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ A.3 Proof for ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) for <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=0</annotation></semantics></math>. The limit point <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\Delta\theta_{\infty}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\Delta\theta_{\infty}\right\rVert_{2}^{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and the first constraint</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\left\{f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})^{(j)}\Big]\Delta\theta_{\infty}\leq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\left\{f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})^{(j)}\Big]\Delta\theta_{\infty}\leq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">and is therefore feasible for the minimization in <a href="#A1.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ A.3 Proof for ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> when <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=0</annotation></semantics></math>. We conclude from the continuity of <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> that <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(\eta_{k})\rightarrow v(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(\eta_{k})\rightarrow v(0)</annotation></semantics></math> and therefore <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> is a minimizer of (<a href="#S2.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ PENEX is Implicit AdaBoost. ‣ 2.3 Relationship to Multi-Class AdaBoost ‣ 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) for <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence the entire sequence <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta_{mk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta_{mk}</annotation></semantics></math> converges to the set of minimizers of (<a href="#S2.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ PENEX is Implicit AdaBoost. ‣ 2.3 Relationship to Multi-Class AdaBoost ‣ 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) for <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=0</annotation></semantics></math>. As a result, <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the Karush-Kuhn-Tucker conditions corresponding to (<a href="#A1.E18" title="Equation 18 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.3 Proof for ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) for <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=0</annotation></semantics></math>. These can be expressed as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta_{\infty}\propto\alpha\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\left\{-\alpha f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})^{(j)}\Big]-\bar{\rho}\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\left\{f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})^{(j)}\Big]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta_{\infty}\propto\alpha\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\left\{-\alpha f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})^{(j)}\Big]-\bar{\rho}\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\left\{f_{\theta_{m-1}}^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}\mathbf{J}(\mathbf{x})^{(j)}\Big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\rho}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\rho}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> is related to a multiplier of the first constraint in <a href="#A1.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ A.3 Proof for ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>. This means that <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta_{\infty}\propto-\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}(\theta_{m-1};\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">PENEX</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta_{\infty}\propto-\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}(\theta_{m-1};\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=\bar{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=\bar{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, which concludes the proof.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Proof for <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1 (Margin Maximization). ‣ 2.1 Theoretical Properties ‣ 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Thm.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a></h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first apply a Chernoff bound to see that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(m_{f}(\mathbf{x},y)\leq\gamma)\,\leq\,\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left\{\beta\left(\gamma+\max_{j\neq y}f^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})-f^{(y)}(\mathbf{x})\right)\right\}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.448em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(m_{f}(\mathbf{x},y)\leq\gamma)\,\leq\,\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left\{\beta\left(\gamma+\max_{j\neq y}f^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})-f^{(y)}(\mathbf{x})\right)\right\}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for any <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we note that for any <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{x},y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{x},y)</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{j\neq y}f^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\;\leq\;\log\left(\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\left\{f^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{j\neq y}f^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\;\leq\;\log\left(\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\left\{f^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\right\}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which we combine with Hölder’s inequality for <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\coloneqq\frac{\beta}{1-\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\coloneqq\frac{\beta}{1-\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">5</span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              We recall that <math id="footnote5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="footnote5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\beta}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\beta}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="footnote5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{1-\beta}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{1-\beta}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a condition for Hölder’s inequality.</span></span></span> to see that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(m_{f}(\mathbf{x},y)\leq\gamma)\;\leq\;e^{\beta\gamma}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle EX}}(f;\,\alpha)]^{1-\beta}\cdot\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{SE}(f)]^{\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">EX</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>SE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(m_{f}(\mathbf{x},y)\leq\gamma)\;\leq\;e^{\beta\gamma}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle EX}}(f;\,\alpha)]^{1-\beta}\cdot\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{SE}(f)]^{\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">We can now apply the weighted AM-GM inequality to get</p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle EX}}(f;\,\alpha)]^{1-\beta}\cdot(\rho\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{SE}(f)])^{\beta}\rho^{-\beta}\;\leq\;((1-\beta)\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle EX}}(f;\,\alpha)]+\beta\rho\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{SE}(f)])\rho^{-\beta}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">EX</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>SE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">EX</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>SE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle EX}}(f;\,\alpha)]^{1-\beta}\cdot(\rho\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{SE}(f)])^{\beta}\rho^{-\beta}\;\leq\;((1-\beta)\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle EX}}(f;\,\alpha)]+\beta\rho\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{SE}(f)])\rho^{-\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">and further, because <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\beta)\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle EX}}(f;\,\alpha)]+\beta\rho\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{SE}(f)]\;\leq\;\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle EX}}(f;\,\alpha)]+\rho\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{SE}(f)]\;=\;\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}(f;\,\alpha,\rho)]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">EX</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>SE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">EX</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>SE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">PENEX</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\beta)\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle EX}}(f;\,\alpha)]+\beta\rho\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{SE}(f)]\;\leq\;\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle EX}}(f;\,\alpha)]+\rho\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{SE}(f)]\;=\;\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}(f;\,\alpha,\rho)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Thus, we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(m_{f}(\mathbf{x},y)\leq\gamma)\;\leq\;e^{\beta\gamma}\rho^{-\beta}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}(f;\,\alpha,\rho)]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">PENEX</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(m_{f}(\mathbf{x},y)\leq\gamma)\;\leq\;e^{\beta\gamma}\rho^{-\beta}\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}(f;\,\alpha,\rho)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.7" class="ltx_p">The result follows from replacing <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\frac{\alpha}{\alpha+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\frac{\alpha}{\alpha+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Stategewise Additive Modeling using a Multi-class Exponential loss</h3>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The standard multi-class AdaBoost solves <a href="#S2.E8" title="In 2.3 Relationship to Multi-Class AdaBoost ‣ 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> via a specific algorithm called SAMME, shown in <a href="#algorithm2" title="In Appendix B Stategewise Additive Modeling using a Multi-class Exponential loss ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Alg.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm2" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span>SAMME (Multi-class AdaBoost)</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm2.4.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Training set <math id="algorithm2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(\mathbf{x}_{i},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(\mathbf{x}_{i},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="algorithm2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{i}\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{i}\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="algorithm2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span>Strong classifier <math id="algorithm2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
            Initialize sample weights <math id="algorithm2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}(i)\leftarrow\frac{1}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}(i)\leftarrow\frac{1}{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="algorithm2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm2.4.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm2.4.4.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm2.4.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> <math id="algorithm2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm2.4.4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
            Fit weak classifier <math id="algorithm2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> using weights <math id="algorithm2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
            Compute weighted error <math id="algorithm2.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\epsilon_{m}\leftarrow\sum_{i=1}^{n}w_{m}(i)\cdot\mathbbm{1}\{g_{m}(\mathbf{x}_{i})\neq y_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">←</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{m}\leftarrow\sum_{i=1}^{n}w_{m}(i)\cdot\mathbbm{1}\{g_{m}(\mathbf{x}_{i})\neq y_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5</span></span>
            Compute classifier weight <math id="algorithm2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{m}\leftarrow\log\left(\frac{1-\epsilon_{m}}{\epsilon_{m}}\right)\,+\,\log(K-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.392em">+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{m}\leftarrow\log\left(\frac{1-\epsilon_{m}}{\epsilon_{m}}\right)\,+\,\log(K-1)</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6</span></span>
            Update sample weights:

<table id="A2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{m+1}(i)\;\leftarrow\;\frac{w_{m}(i)\exp(-\eta_{m}\mathbbm{1}\{g_{m}(\mathbf{x}_{i})\neq y_{i}\})}{Z_{m}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≠</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{m+1}(i)\;\leftarrow\;\frac{w_{m}(i)\exp(-\eta_{m}\mathbbm{1}\{g_{m}(\mathbf{x}_{i})\neq y_{i}\})}{Z_{m}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7</span></span>
            where <math id="algorithm2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is the partition function

</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8</span></span>
            end for
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">9</span></span>
            Combine weak classifiers: <math id="algorithm2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{M}(\mathbf{x})=\arg\max_{k\in[K]}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\eta_{m}g_{m}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{M}(\mathbf{x})=\arg\max_{k\in[K]}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\eta_{m}g_{m}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>


</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Practical Implementation of PENEX</h3>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Inference</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Motivated by the Fisher consistency result (<a href="#S2.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 2.1 (Fisher Consistency). ‣ 2.1 Theoretical Properties ‣ 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Prop.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>), we always rescale logits that are optimized on PENEX by <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, to obtain a prediction <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}_{\scriptscriptstyle\textrm{PENEX}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext mathsize="0.710em">PENEX</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}_{\scriptscriptstyle\textrm{PENEX}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we always use</p>
<table id="A3.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}_{\scriptscriptstyle\textrm{PENEX}}(y\,|\,\mathbf{x})\;\coloneqq\;\frac{\exp\{(1-\alpha)f^{(y)}(\mathbf{x})\}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\{(1-\alpha)f^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext mathsize="0.710em">PENEX</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}_{\scriptscriptstyle\textrm{PENEX}}(y\,|\,\mathbf{x})\;\coloneqq\;\frac{\exp\{(1-\alpha)f^{(y)}(\mathbf{x})\}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\{(1-\alpha)f^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})\}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{(j)}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> are the logits obtained by optimizing <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">PENEX</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle PENEX}}</annotation></semantics></math> <a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Default Value for Sensitivity <math id="A3.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While the optimal choice of sensitivity <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> depends on various factors such as training set size, model architecture, amount of classes and label noise, we notice that the tuned value for <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is typically close to</p>
<table id="A3.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\;=\;0.1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.558em">=</mo><mn> 0.1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\;=\;0.1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">If PENEX is used without tuning, we generally recommend <a href="#A3.E21" title="In C.2 Default Value for Sensitivity 𝛼 ‣ Appendix C Practical Implementation of PENEX ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a> as the default choice. If, however, there is substantial label noise, we recommend a smaller value. If there is little label noise, <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> may be chosen larger, leading to more aggressive margin maximization.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Default Values for <a href="#algorithm1" title="In 2.2 Practical Implementation ‣ 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Alg.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h4>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all experiments conducted in the present work, we use the following hyper parameter configuration:</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.SS3.tab1" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A3.SS3.tab1.1" class="ltx_logical-block">
            
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent ltx_align_center">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:166.6pt;height:50pt;vertical-align:-22.5pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameter</span></span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Value</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">EMA factor <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1.1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Lower penalty bound <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\mathrm{min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\mathrm{min}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1.1.1.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1.1.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_t">Upper penalty bound <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\mathrm{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\mathrm{max}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1.1.1.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_t"><math id="A3.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100.0</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></p>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In practice, we observe in all conducted experiments that results typically do not differ much if these parameters are chosen differently.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>PyTorch-like Code</h4>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As mentioned in <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2 Practical Implementation ‣ 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>, PENEX does not require a custom training loop in order to implement <a href="#algorithm1" title="In 2.2 Practical Implementation ‣ 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Alg.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. A PyTorch-like loss module is displayed in <a href="#A3.F5" title="In C.4 PyTorch-like Code ‣ Appendix C Practical Implementation of PENEX ‣ Appendix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, with only 34 lines of code (including comments). It is easy to see that it can be integrated seamlessly into any standard training loop.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F5" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.F5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="43.38" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 675 43.38" width="675"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,43.38) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.43 L 0 34.95 C 0 39.6 3.77 43.38 8.43 43.38 L 666.57 43.38 C 671.23 43.38 675 39.6 675 34.95 L 675 8.43 C 675 3.77 671.23 0 666.57 0 L 8.43 0 C 3.77 0 0 3.77 0 8.43 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F4F9FF;" fill="#F4F9FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.55 8.43 L 0.55 34.95 C 0.55 39.3 4.08 42.82 8.43 42.82 L 666.57 42.82 C 670.92 42.82 674.45 39.3 674.45 34.95 L 674.45 8.43 C 674.45 4.08 670.92 0.55 666.57 0.55 L 8.43 0.55 C 4.08 0.55 0.55 4.08 0.55 8.43 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 8.43 9.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:47.56em;--ltx-fo-height:1.95em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="29.67" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 26.98)" width="658.1"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
