</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Experimental Details</h3>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Libraries</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For our implementation, we use <span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PyTorch Lightning</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Falcon &amp; The PyTorch Lightning team, 2019</a>)</cite>, a framework built on top of <span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PyTorch</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Paszke et al., 2019</a>)</cite>. For all experiments involving language models, we use the <span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">transformers</span>, <span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">datasets</span> and <span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">evaluate</span> Hugging Face libraries. For hyperparameter tuning, we use the <span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Optuna</span> library <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Akiba et al., 2019</a>)</cite>. We use <span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SciencePlots</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Garrett, 2021</a>)</cite> for appealing plots and <a href="https://github.com/wandb/wandb" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href ltx_font_typewriter">weights &amp; biases</a> for development and analysis.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Dataset &amp; Model Licenses</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The licenses of each dataset and pretrained model used in the present work are listed in the following table:</p>
</div>
