</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Ablation Implementations</h4>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To take the zero-sum constraint in CONEX <a href="#S2.Ex1" title="In 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> into account, we first define the constraint</p>
<table id="A4.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(\mathbf{x};\,\theta)\coloneqq\mathbf{1}^{\top}f_{\theta}(\mathbf{x})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(\mathbf{x};\,\theta)\coloneqq\mathbf{1}^{\top}f_{\theta}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and see that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(\mathbf{x};\,\theta)=0,\;\forall\mathbf{x}\in\text{supp}(P)\;\iff\;\mathbb{E}[h(\mathbf{x};\,\theta)^{2}]=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(\mathbf{x};\,\theta)=0,\;\forall\mathbf{x}\in\text{supp}(P)\;\iff\;\mathbb{E}[h(\mathbf{x};\,\theta)^{2}]=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Squared Penalty.</h6>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We penalize deviations from the penalty constraint via a quadratic penalty. To this end, we construct the loss function</p>
<table id="A4.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\theta_{m})\;=\;\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle EX}}(\theta_{m})+\frac{\rho}{2}\Big(\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[h(\mathbf{x};\,\theta_{m})^{2}\right]\Big)^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">EX</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\theta_{m})\;=\;\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle EX}}(\theta_{m})+\frac{\rho}{2}\Big(\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[h(\mathbf{x};\,\theta_{m})^{2}\right]\Big)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">the optimum of which converges to the constrained solution for <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math> (for a fixed learning rate <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>). In practice, however, choosing large <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> leads to an ill-conditioned loss surface, which is why a trade-off must be made in the choice of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Augmented Lagrangian.</h6>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The augmented Lagrangian method <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hestenes, 1969</a>)</cite> considers an objective that arises from <a href="#S2.Ex1" title="In 2 Penalized Exponential Loss (PENEX)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> by introducing a penalty term with parameter <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and the dual variable <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{m}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{m}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{L}(\theta_{m})\;\coloneqq\;\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle EX}}(\theta_{m})\,+\,\frac{\rho}{2}\Big(\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[h(\mathbf{x};\,\theta_{m})^{2}\right]\Big)^{2}\,+\,\lambda_{m}\Big(\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[h(\mathbf{x};\,\theta_{m})^{2}\right]\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">EX</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.392em">+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.392em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{L}(\theta_{m})\;\coloneqq\;\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{\scriptscriptstyle EX}}(\theta_{m})\,+\,\frac{\rho}{2}\Big(\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[h(\mathbf{x};\,\theta_{m})^{2}\right]\Big)^{2}\,+\,\lambda_{m}\Big(\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[h(\mathbf{x};\,\theta_{m})^{2}\right]\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The algorithm updates the primal (<math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>) and dual (<math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>) variables in an alternating fashion:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{m}\leftarrow\theta_{m-1}-\eta\nabla_{\theta}\mathscr{L}(\theta_{m-1}),\qquad\lambda_{m}\leftarrow\lambda_{m-1}\;+\;\frac{\rho}{\nu}\Big(\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[h(\mathbf{x};\,\theta_{m-1})^{2}\right]\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mi>ν</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{m}\leftarrow\theta_{m-1}-\eta\nabla_{\theta}\mathscr{L}(\theta_{m-1}),\qquad\lambda_{m}\leftarrow\lambda_{m-1}\;+\;\frac{\rho}{\nu}\Big(\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[h(\mathbf{x};\,\theta_{m-1})^{2}\right]\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is an inverse scaling factor.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Note</span>: In practice, computing <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> would require loading the entire training set into memory. We thus resort to sub-sampling <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> from batches.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Metrics</h4>

<section id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Accuracy.</h6>

<div id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We measure the accuracy of a classifier <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A4.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{ACC}(f)\;\coloneqq\;\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbbm{1}\Big\{y_{i}\;=\;\arg\max_{j}f^{(j)}(\mathbf{x}_{i})\Big\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>ACC</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≔</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mi>arg</mi><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></munder><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ACC}(f)\;\coloneqq\;\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbbm{1}\Big\{y_{i}\;=\;\arg\max_{j}f^{(j)}(\mathbf{x}_{i})\Big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Expected Calibration Error.</h6>

<div id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Formally, it is given as</p>
<table id="A4.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ECE}(f)\;\coloneqq\;\sum_{m=1}^{M}\frac{|B_{m}|}{n}\big|\text{ACC}(f;\,B_{m})-\text{CONF}(f;\,B_{m})\big|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>ECE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">≔</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>ACC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>CONF</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ECE}(f)\;\coloneqq\;\sum_{m=1}^{M}\frac{|B_{m}|}{n}\big|\text{ACC}(f;\,B_{m})-\text{CONF}(f;\,B_{m})\big|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of data points whose prediction confidence falls into the interval</p>
<table id="A4.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{m}\;\coloneqq\;\Big(\frac{m-1}{M};\,\frac{m}{M}\Big]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≔</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo rspace="0.337em">;</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}\;\coloneqq\;\Big(\frac{m-1}{M};\,\frac{m}{M}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A4.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CONF}(f)\;\coloneqq\;\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\hat{P}(y_{i}\;|\;f(\mathbf{x}_{i}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>CONF</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CONF}(f)\;\coloneqq\;\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\hat{P}(y_{i}\;|\;f(\mathbf{x}_{i})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">We use the default <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=15</annotation></semantics></math>, as implemented by the <a href="https://lightning.ai/docs/torchmetrics/stable/classification/calibration_error.html" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">torchmetrics</a> library.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Brier Score.</h6>

<div id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compute the Brier score as</p>
<table id="A4.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{BRIER}(f)\;\coloneqq\;\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{K}\left(\hat{P}(y=j\;|\;f(\mathbf{x}_{i}))-\mathbf{y}^{(j)}_{i}\right)^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>BRIER</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{BRIER}(f)\;\coloneqq\;\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{K}\left(\hat{P}(y=j\;|\;f(\mathbf{x}_{i}))-\mathbf{y}^{(j)}_{i}\right)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A4.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}^{(j)}_{i}\;\coloneqq\;\begin{cases}1,\quad\text{if}\;\;j=y_{i}\\
0,\quad\text{else,}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.560em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>else,</mtext></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}^{(j)}_{i}\;\coloneqq\;\begin{cases}1,\quad\text{if}\;\;j=y_{i}\\
0,\quad\text{else,}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">is a one-hot encoding of the label.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.6 </span>Data Preprocessing</h4>

<section id="A4.SS6.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.6.1 </span>Computer Vision</h5>

<div id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We do not perform data augmentation for any computer vision task.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS6.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">CIFAR-10/CIFAR-100/PathMNIST.</h6>

<div id="A4.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We perform standard normalization for these datasets, with the following mean and standard deviation values</p>
<table id="A4.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=(0.5,0.5,0.5),\;\sigma=(0.5,0.5,0.5)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=(0.5,0.5,0.5),\;\sigma=(0.5,0.5,0.5),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where we have three values for each parameter because standardization is applied per channel (there are three channels). For PathMNIST in particular, prior to standardization, we load the dataset at a resolution of <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64\times 64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64\times 64</annotation></semantics></math> and further scale it down to <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32\times 32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32\times 32</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS6.SSS1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">ImageNet.</h6>

<div id="A4.SS6.SSS1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS1.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We also perform normalization, but instead with the following (standard) values</p>
<table id="A4.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=(0.485,0.456,0.406),\;\sigma=(0.229,0.224,0.225)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.485</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.456</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.406</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.229</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.224</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.225</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=(0.485,0.456,0.406),\;\sigma=(0.229,0.224,0.225).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS1.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In addition, as common with vision transformers, we apply the following data augmentations: images are first resized to 256 pixels along the shorter side, then randomly cropped to <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="224\times 224" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>224</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>224</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">224\times 224</annotation></semantics></math> pixels with a scale factor uniformly sampled between <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.8</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>, followed by a random horizontal flip with probability <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS6.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.6.2 </span>Fine-Tuning RoBERTa</h5>

<div id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There exist five labels in total corresponding to the categories tech, business, sport, entertainment and politics. To prevent memory overload, the input length is limited to a maximum length of <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>512</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">512</annotation></semantics></math> tokens and text is clipped if this length is exceeded (this is fairly common in other works, e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kladny et al. (2025)</a></cite>). An example text input for the label <span id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">business</span> is demonstrated in the following:</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T2" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span><span id="A4.T2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Affects of the Sensitivity Parameter on Validation Curves.</span> Smaller <math id="A4.T2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> typically lead to faster convergence, but worse generalization toward the end of the training duration (as can be seen more clearly for CIFAR-100). In addition, for very large <math id="A4.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=3.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=3.2</annotation></semantics></math>, training curves tend to become less stable.</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<table id="A4.T2.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_figure_panel">
<tr id="A4.T2.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T2.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.T2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:487.8pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.tab1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<span id="A4.T2.tab1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle ltx_listing"><span class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="bbc˙news.txt">⬇</a></span>
